					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607460281" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1503118332 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Aug 2017 04:52</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3573901">
									

<p>Took a look at this in chat, not totally loving the sheer amount of fluff information, but I can respect the amount of time and effort put into that supplement stuff.</p>
<p>However, am downvoting for the numerous small errors:</p>
<ul>
<li>&quot;Translated texts written by SCP-XXXX-1 has&quot; &gt; either &quot;texts written have&quot; or &quot;text written has&quot;</li>
<li>&quot;the artificial constructs created by said population (SCP-XXXX-2). / SCP-XXXX-2 are the artificial constructs of SCP-XXXX-1&quot; &gt; overly repetitive</li>
<li>The SCP-XXXX-1 sub-designation paragraph should go before the XXXX-2 one. It makes more sense from a logical and narrative reading perspective.</li>
<li>&quot;in an isolated instance of SCP-XXXX-2 (henceforth referred to as SCP-XXXX-2A)&quot; &gt; this belongs in the description. Not having the sub-designation introduced in the description makes it harder for a reader to process all the information.</li>
<li>&quot;society that SCP-XXXX-1 lives in appears to function similarly to feudal societies societies such as those of medieval Europe or Japan&quot; &gt; again, repetitive, and a bit run-on. I'd use &quot;feudal systems&quot;. Also, medieval Europe and medieval Japan have some significant differences. If the main takeaway here is the caste system, I'd pick just one to reference and note that the &quot;society functions using a caste system similar to that of [place] during [time period]&quot;.</li>
<li>&quot;SCP-XXXX-1 have a typical lifespan of 215 days and will often seek out areas of sun to occupy.&quot; &gt; use of &quot;occupy&quot; seems a little off here, especially since it's not clear to me as a reader how the fact about sunlight occupation is related to lifespan. Also, you might want to specify &quot;sunlit areas&quot; rather than just &quot;area of sun&quot; since that's a little colloquial.</li>
<li>&quot;SCP-XXXX-1 use a form of basic currency for purchasing basic goods&quot; &gt; again, repetitive. Try substituting &quot;simple&quot; for the first &quot;basic&quot;.</li>
<li>And so on.</li>
</ul>
<p>As I stated in chat, this isn't quite my type of article. However, I do believe it could benefit from some more polishing up for professionalism.</p>

