			<div class="content" id="post-content-3574085">
									

<p>I have a lot of respect for the tremendous amount of world building that clearly went into this - it was obviously a labor of love. As such, I can't bring myself to downvote it, though I feel (as others have already said) that it doesn't really work as an SCP; it's good writing that I think is just in the wrong place.</p>
<p>These little guys seem like a solid piece of a larger fantasy setting (like something from the Wanderer's Library), more than a stand-alone piece of fiction. There's a ton of well-written information here, but I found myself skimming through, looking for some kind of twist or punchline.</p>
<p>That said, even though this isn't to my taste, I'm voting neutral and rooting for it to survive; the foundation-verse is big and wide, with room for pretty much anything, and I bet enough people will &quot;get&quot; this to keep it out of the negatives.</p>

							</div>

								
					
